      "reason": "generate_cursor allocated sizeof(cursor_obj), the pointer size, instead of the complete Cursor object. Actual constructor writes beyond its returned allocation into a protected page (RED); allocating sizeof(*cursor_obj) preserves original initialized center/image and passes (GREEN). Original browser cursor/menu interaction failed; corrected actual gameplay works."
    },
    {
      "file": "proj/src/highscore.c",
      "originalSha256": "016c6483afd297ca139913705eefa8b6c5b93d0f78fc99aa6a18cc81e71867ce",
      "patchedSha256": "d81b494fa7689b04208b252050050be9d9d689fa9e61f1018444a5a107f4096a",
      "reason": "load_highscores read names without width and looped beyond its five owned slots, including after normal trailing newline. Bound records to MAX_HIGHSCORES, scan at most5name characters and store only complete triples. Actual owner with real temporary score files and guard pages RED beyond table, GREEN preserving sorted names/times/scores and rejecting incomplete oversized names."
    }
